# [The Ossuary](ossuary_doc)

A relic interior authored as data - the same structure `relic_layout.py` builds in
Python, written the way a mission author would write it.

Open it with **Artemis AMD: Show Relic Plan** to see the floor plan, and drag a chamber
to move it. Every drag rewrites one line of this file and nothing else, so this prose
survives being edited around.

## [Relics](relics)

### [The Ossuary](ossuary)
---
Loc: 0, 0, 0
Atmosphere: purple
Containment: tractor
Scrape band: 120
Margin: 60
Forbid jump: yes
---
An ancient thing, hollow, and not built by anyone still alive. Nothing about its shape
suggests a builder who breathed.

Two rules shape the numbers below: neighbouring chambers stay under ~3500u apart, because
`render-distance-objects` is 5000 and a wider relic stops drawing its own far side; and
the whole thing stays under ~11200u across so its atmosphere fits in one nebula.

### [hub](hub)
---
Relic: ossuary
Chamber: 0, 0, 0, 900
Passage to: gallery 300, shaft 240, spine 300
---
Where you arrive. Three ways out.

